Priority: 1
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-multi-select

Goal:
Replace the current stroke-focused undo logic with real action-based canvas history that supports undo and redo for all important canvas edits, not just drawing.

Context:
The user confirmed that `Ctrl+Z` works for simple stroke undo but fails as a general history system, especially for delete and restore flows. The current behavior appears to be tied too closely to stroke-list mutation. The app now needs a real action log or equivalent undo/redo model that can reverse and reapply user-intent edits across item types.

Expected changes:

- inspect the current canvas history implementation and identify where it assumes stroke-only operations
- add redo support in addition to undo
- make history cover at least:
  - drawing strokes
  - deleting selected items
  - recoloring selected vector items
  - pasting images
  - resizing items
  - text content edits
- ensure history works for mixed canvas item types, not just strokes
- update keyboard handling so redo has an explicit shortcut path in addition to undo

Acceptance criteria:

- Undo and redo work for draw, delete, recolor, paste-image, resize, and text-content changes.
- Undo after deleting an item restores it instead of losing it permanently.
- Redo reapplies the undone action correctly.
- The implementation is clearly action- or snapshot-based around user edits rather than a stroke-only side list.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Favor one coherent history model instead of per-feature one-off undo exceptions.
- Keep scope on Canvas Mode behavior only.
- If some low-level edit path cannot be made undoable in the same slice, document the exact gap explicitly in the task report.
